+
+## Amendment: settings are build inputs for Cargo too (2026-11-14, #1751)
+
+The output plan's read list now includes the Cargo.toml its Settings reader
+parsed. Cargo's dep-info callback and the standalone compile record both
+consume this same list; the standalone driver's separate addition is removed.
+A metadata-only runner edit therefore invalidates the prior Cargo test build.
+No source touch or cache deletion is required, and no second settings parser
+is introduced. ADR 0262 case C: generated test imports and actual execution
+must follow the requested runner, rather than stale build state.
+
+The regression runs a crate under Node, changes only its runner metadata to
+Bun and back, and checks both runner outcomes and generated imports. The
+mutation removes the settings input and must fail that regression and the
+existing standalone-record check.
